1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:10,966
This is Agent Kontrol. It's one screen for every AI agent
I run. Claude Code, Cowork, ChatGPT, and Hermes. Who's
working, who's stuck, and who needs me.

2
00:00:10,966 --> 00:00:19,603
Right now, Claude Code on my MacBook is waiting on
permission to push. That's the one I need to look at.

3
00:00:19,603 --> 00:00:24,373
Below the cards, live activity shows every milestone as it
happens.

4
00:00:24,373 --> 00:00:32,241
History keeps every session and every event, so I can see
what each agent did while I was away.

5
00:00:32,241 --> 00:00:39,335
Progress answers a harder question. Is the backlog
actually shrinking? Merged pull requests alone won't tell
you.

6
00:00:39,335 --> 00:00:50,689
And this is the Gibson. The same fleet, in 3D. Agents
stand on the outer ring, grouped by machine. Towers are
projects, and every floor is a task.

7
00:00:50,689 --> 00:00:54,047
Drag to orbit around the whole fleet.

8
00:00:57,524 --> 00:01:06,293
Or let it rotate on its own, like a status board on the
wall.

9
00:01:08,290 --> 00:01:14,940
Zoom in, and the dashed lines show which agent is working
on which project.

10
00:01:14,940 --> 00:01:21,293
Click an agent to see its details. That orange beacon
means it's waiting on me.

11
00:01:21,816 --> 00:01:28,927
Agent Kontrol is open source and self-hosted, on Neon or
any Postgres. Narration is an AI voice.
